data.content:
Build is clean. Here's a summary of all **5 breaking changes** identified and fixed:

---

### Fixes applied to this project

| # | Breaking Change | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | **TFM & packages** → `net8.0`/`8.0.0` | Updated to `net9.0`/`9.0.0` |
| 2 | **`HasData` with `DateTime.UtcNow`** — non-deterministic seed data causes `Migrate()` to throw "pending model changes" | Replaced with fixed constant `new DateTime(2024,1,1,0,0,0,DateTimeKind.Utc)` |
| 3 | **`Migrate()` inside explicit transaction** — now throws because EF Core 9 manages its own transactions | Removed the wrapping `CreateExecutionStrategy`/`BeginTransaction`/`Commit` |
| 4 | **Design package** — SDK 9.0.200+ can't find it with old `PrivateAssets="all"` shorthand | Added explicit `<IncludeAssets>` and `<Publish>true</Publish>` |

### Fixes needed in your Cosmos DB project

Since the Cosmos DB project isn't in this directory, here are the exact fixes to apply there:

**5. Discriminator renamed to `$type`** — existing documents use `"Discriminator"`:
```csharp
// In OnModelCreating, preserve the old property name:
modelBuilder.Entity<YourEntity>().HasDiscriminator<string>("Discriminator");
```

**6. `id` property no longer contains discriminator** — existing docs have `"EntityType|Key"` format:
```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<YourEntity>().HasRootDiscriminatorInJsonId(true);
```

**7. Sync I/O no longer supported** — `ToList()`, `SaveChanges()`, etc. now throw:
```csharp
// Before (throws in EF Core 9 Cosmos)
var items = db.Products.ToList();
db.SaveChanges();

// After
var items = await db.Products.ToListAsync();
await db.SaveChangesAsync();
```
